@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Release Pipelines";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Release Pipelines in Azure DevOps enable teams to automate software deployments, ensuring reliable, repeatable, and efficient delivery to production and other environments.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is a Release Pipeline?</h2>
        <p>A **Release Pipeline** automates the deployment of applications to different environments such as **development, staging, and production**.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Ensures **consistent deployments** across multiple environments.</li>
            <li>Reduces **manual deployment errors**.</li>
            <li>Enables **approval workflows** for controlled releases.</li>
            <li>Supports **multi-stage deployments** with rollback capabilities.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/release-pipeline.png" alt="Azure Release Pipeline" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps Release Pipeline Workflow</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Release Pipeline Workflow</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Build artifacts are created and stored in **Azure Artifacts**.</li>
                <li>The release pipeline picks up artifacts and **deploys them to environments**.</li>
                <li>Pre-deployment approvals are triggered before moving to the next stage.</li>
                <li>Post-deployment validations and monitoring ensure success.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Creating a Release Pipeline in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to set up a release pipeline:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Go to Pipelines > Releases:</strong> Click "New Release Pipeline".</li>
            <li><strong>Select a Template:</strong> Choose a built-in template or create a custom pipeline.</li>
            <li><strong>Add Artifacts:</strong> Select build artifacts generated from the CI pipeline.</li>
            <li><strong>Define Stages:</strong> Configure environments (Dev, Staging, Production).</li>
            <li><strong>Set up Deployment Tasks:</strong> Add tasks for deployments (Azure App Service, Kubernetes, etc.).</li>
            <li><strong>Enable Approvals:</strong> Configure manual approvals for controlled releases.</li>
            <li><strong>Save and Deploy:</strong> Start deployment and monitor logs.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML for a Release Pipeline</h4>
            <pre>
stages:
- stage: Deploy
  jobs:
  - deployment: DeployToAzure
    environment: 'Production'
    strategy:
      runOnce:
        deploy:
          steps:
          - task: AzureWebApp@1
            inputs:
              azureSubscription: 'AzureServiceConnection'
              appName: 'my-web-app'
              package: '$(Pipeline.Workspace)/drop/*.zip'
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/release-pipeline-stages.png" alt="Stages in Release Pipeline" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Stages in Azure DevOps Release Pipeline</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Release Pipelines</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **staging environments** before deploying to production.</li>
            <li>Enable **pre-deployment approvals** for controlled rollouts.</li>
            <li>Monitor releases using **Application Insights**.</li>
            <li>Implement **rollback strategies** for failed deployments.</li>
            <li>Automate **post-deployment validations** to ensure reliability.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Release Pipelines in Azure DevOps simplify and automate the **deployment process**, ensuring efficiency, reliability, and security. By integrating **approval workflows, monitoring, and rollback strategies**, teams can deliver high-quality software seamlessly.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Stages, Jobs & Tasks in Release Pipelines**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("StagesJobsTasks", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Stages, Jobs & Tasks &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
